{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/643314?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/643314?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/643314?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/643314?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/643314?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/643314?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A643314"}, "created": "2004-01-27T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2024-11-14T18:19:06.778992+00:00", "metadata": {"publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "70", "artid": "054015", "year": 2004, "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "authors": [{"full_name": "Bauer, Christian W."}, {"full_name": "Pirjol, Dan"}, {"full_name": "Rothstein, Ira Z."}, {"full_name": "Stewart, Iain W."}], "texkeys": ["Bauer:2004tj"], "abstracts": [{"value": "Using the soft-collinear effective theory we derive the factorization theorem for the decays B-> M1 M2 with M{1,2}= pi,K, rho,K*, at leading order in Lambda/E_M and Lambda/mb. The results derived here apply even if alpha_s(E_M Lambda) is not perturbative, and we prove that the physics sensitive to the E*Lambda scale is the same in B-> M1 M2 and B-> M form factors. We argue that c-cbar penguins could give long-distance effects at leading order. Decays to two transversely polarized vector mesons are discussed. Analyzing B-> pi pi we find predictions for B^0 -> pi^0 pi^0 and |V_{ub}| f_+(0) as a function of gamma."}], "control_number": 643314, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.70.054015"}], "arxiv_eprints": [{"value": "hep-ph/0401188"}], "titles": [{"title": "B ---> M(1) M(2): Factorization, charming penguins, strong phases, and polarization"}, {"title": "B --> M(1) M(2): Factorization, charming penguins, strong phases, and polarization."}], "author_count": 4, "document_type": ["article"]}, "id": "643314"}], "t